WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.050
A twenty-five minute site visit shouldn't cost you an hour at a desk.

00:00:05.949 --> 00:00:09.700
Open a Quick Report and pick your survey template.

00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:14.083
Choose the policyholder and the property you just walked.

00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:21.183
Drop in your survey photos. Tick the ones that show a hazard, and those get a written finding and a recommendation.

00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:27.233
Then just talk through the building, the same order you already inspect in.

00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:43.933
Inspector: "Front view. Masonry construction, three stories, six units, two per floor. Walkway at the main entrance is cracked and heaved, trip hazard. Basement electrical panel, older breakers, evidence of overheating."

00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:46.133
Hit generate.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:53.199
Construction, occupancy and every condition you described land in the right section of your template.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:01:00.349
And each hazard gets standard recommendation language your underwriters already expect.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.399
Review it, confirm it, and submit.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:10.466
Out comes a clean, branded report, ready for the carrier.

00:01:13.316 --> 00:01:20.366
Site visit to carrier-ready report, before you are back in the car. Book a demo, and bring one of your own reports.
